web-digest Repository Version History
=====================================

v1.1.1 (Release Date: TBD)
--------------------------
- Fixed side-panel opening and per-tab run-state cleanup races so a run stays
  bound to its target tab and stale state cannot return after navigation or
  tab closure.

v1.1.0 (2026-08-31)
-------------------
- Added an opt-in "Summarize in Japanese" setting; off by default, summaries
  continue to use the page's own language.
- Added OpenAI and Claude alongside Sakura AI Engine as selectable AI providers,
  with independent credentials and models per provider. Sakura remains the default
  and existing Sakura settings continue to work without migration.
- Raised the per-request material budget from 40,000 to 200,000 characters,
  so substantially larger pages can use the one-request path before staged
  summarization is needed.

v1.0.1 (2026-08-26)
-------------------
- Aligned the supported Chrome version with what opening the side panel actually requires.
- Stopped work that finishes after its tab was closed from restoring the removed session state.
- Prevented summaries from starting when their side panel could not be opened.

v1.0.0 (2026-08-16)
-------------------
- Initial release.

Version History Guidelines
==========================
- Write one coherent change per physical line, as a rule.
- Keep entries near 100 columns where practical. Necessary file names, API
  names, constant names, and setting names may extend an entry to
  approximately 120 columns.
- When a version history already exists, balance a new entry against the
  length of the existing lines, so that the whole file stays consistent.
  Holding to the form this file has settled on comes before the one physical
  line above, and leaves that rule standing wherever no such form exists.
- When an entry becomes substantially longer, omit or abstract implementation
  details, examples, reasons, and secondary effects where possible.
- Preserve the changed target, externally observable behavior, compatibility
  or privacy and security impact, and important setting or constant names.
- Combine related changes within the same version, especially changes to the
  same file or feature.
- Place closely related entries near each other.
- Append an independent new change to the end of the current version entry.
- An unreleased entry carries (Release Date: TBD). Replacing TBD with the
  actual date is the release itself, and is not a change to record here.
- This file records the history of the repository. A change that is not
  observable from outside does not need an entry here, and a documentation
  only change takes none unless its scale makes it worth one line saying so.
